  "step_3": "The decision reason requires considering the differences between outcomes and a reference value (zero in this case), computing the mean difference (i.e., expected value), and preferring the lottery with the more favorable mean difference. In this case, both lotteries have the same expected value (2700), so the reason would be indifferent. However, the individual does not mention expected value, differences from zero, or any calculation involving mean differences. Instead, the individual relies on a subjective interpretation of probability — perceiving 90% as nearly certain and 45% as nearly 50/50 — and frames the choice based on risk aversion. The individual does not apply the rule of comparing mean differences from zero. Therefore, the decision reason was not used. The individual's reasoning is based on risk perception and probability misestimation, not on the formal rule of the decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
}

